{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463276",
      "title": "v-if, v-else and v-else-if",
      "lectureOrder": 44,
      "videoOrder": 39,
      "sourceHash": "09ffb49800c4a3ff8f6e18a936d115264a076f30944f8cdb46fc024f182b96fb",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 4.05,
          "en": "There are a couple of things that are worth knowing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.05,
          "end": 8.13,
          "en": "about v-if. For one, you can have any expression in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.13,
          "end": 10.78,
          "en": "that deals a truthy or falsy value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.78,
          "end": 13.26,
          "en": "just as in a regular if statement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.26,
          "end": 16.01,
          "en": "In here, you can also check whatever you want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.01,
          "end": 18.89,
          "en": "and it will be interpreted as truthy or falsy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.89,
          "end": 21.18,
          "en": "by JavaScript. You can, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.18,
          "end": 26.18,
          "en": "also combine conditions here with end, or or, that works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.51,
          "end": 30.02,
          "en": "You can also point at a computed property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.02,
          "end": 32.54,
          "en": "you can point at a data property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.54,
          "end": 34.13,
          "en": "you can execute a method here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.13,
          "end": 38.27,
          "en": "as long as that method returns a truthy or falsy value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.27,
          "end": 39.733,
          "en": "That is all possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.64,
          "end": 44.23,
          "en": "But besides that, which should be fairly obvious,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.23,
          "end": 48.09,
          "en": "since it's really just like if in your HTML code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.09,
          "end": 52.46,
          "en": "so it works like if in JavaScript just in HTML.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.46,
          "end": 56.01,
          "en": "But besides that, there also is another directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.01,
          "end": 59.56,
          "en": "you can use in conjunction with v-if. Because, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.56,
          "end": 63.31,
          "en": "we don't just want to show this paragraph conditionally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.31,
          "end": 66.09,
          "en": "we also want to show the list conditionally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.09,
          "end": 70.6,
          "en": "And, we only want to show this list if we do have goals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.6,
          "end": 72.59,
          "en": "That means we can add v-if if on that too,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.59,
          "end": 76.03999999999999,
          "en": "and we can check if goals length is greater than zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.03999999999999,
          "end": 78.49,
          "en": "Because only if it's greater than zero,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.49,
          "end": 81.13,
          "en": "only then we want to show this list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.13,
          "end": 82.39,
          "en": "If we save and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.39,
          "end": 84.993,
          "en": "we therefore only see the paragraph initially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.98,
          "end": 87.83,
          "en": "But if I then add a goal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.83,
          "end": 89.85,
          "en": "the paragraph disappears. And instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.85,
          "end": 92.863,
          "en": "we see the list with that dummy goal initially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.67,
          "end": 97.57,
          "en": "This works and there's nothing wrong with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.57,
          "end": 101.64,
          "en": "But, essentially, this is a little bit like the else case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.64,
          "end": 103.7,
          "en": "in a JavaScript if statement, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.7,
          "end": 107.06,
          "en": "And, there you can also have else and even else if.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.06,
          "end": 109.12299999999999,
          "en": "That's all supported in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.03,
          "end": 114.52000000000001,
          "en": "And, Vue also supports this in HTML with its directives.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.52000000000001,
          "end": 117.78999999999999,
          "en": "Instead of repeating v-if here, which you can do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.78999999999999,
          "end": 121.83,
          "en": "But instead of doing that, you can also specify v-else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.83,
          "end": 125.88,
          "en": "The only important thing is that v-else has to be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.88,
          "end": 129.36,
          "en": "on an element that comes directly after",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.36,
          "end": 131.87,
          "en": "an element with v-if on it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.87,
          "end": 134.32,
          "en": "You can't have another element in between.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.32,
          "end": 136.38,
          "en": "If we have a paragraph in between,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.38,
          "end": 137.773,
          "en": "that would not work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 138.66,
          "end": 143.66,
          "en": "V-else needs to be used on a direct neighbor element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.75,
          "end": 145.72,
          "en": "of the element which has v-if.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 145.72,
          "end": 148.96,
          "en": "This works, an element in between breaks it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 148.96,
          "end": 150.45,
          "en": "But with that I can reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 151.32999999999998,
          "end": 153.653,
          "en": "and get the same behavior as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 154.53,
          "end": 156.46,
          "en": "Now, sometimes you also have scenarios",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 156.46,
          "end": 159.74,
          "en": "where you have multiple possible conditions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 159.74,
          "end": 163.67000000000002,
          "en": "And, that's why you'll also have a v-else-if condition,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 163.67000000000002,
          "end": 166.28,
          "en": "where you can check if goals length is, let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 166.28,
          "end": 170.27,
          "en": "greater than zero. And, then you could have another element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 170.27,
          "end": 172.81,
          "en": "with v-else in case that's not met,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 172.81,
          "end": 177.05,
          "en": "and that's not met with your fallback content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 177.05,
          "end": 180.37,
          "en": "In this case, that would kick in for a negative length,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 180.37,
          "end": 182.06,
          "en": "which, of course, can't occur,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 182.06,
          "end": 184.88,
          "en": "but I'm just showing this as an example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 184.88,
          "end": 189.88,
          "en": "So, v-if, v-else-if and v-else can be used to control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 190.52,
          "end": 194.14,
          "en": "which parts of your HTML code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 194.14,
          "end": 197.69,
          "en": "are really showing up on the final page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 197.69,
          "end": 199.32,
          "en": "And, I want to emphasize",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 199.32,
          "end": 202,
          "en": "that it's not just about showing and hiding stuff.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 202,
          "end": 205.47,
          "en": "It's really about including those elements in the DOM",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 205.47,
          "end": 206.82999999999998,
          "en": "or not including them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 206.82999999999998,
          "end": 210.17000000000002,
          "en": "It's really about attaching and detaching.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 210.17000000000002,
          "end": 212.69,
          "en": "If you inspect this paragraph,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 212.69,
          "end": 217.17000000000002,
          "en": "you, of course, see that this paragraph is there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 217.17000000000002,
          "end": 218.863,
          "en": "but there is no list below it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 219.8,
          "end": 223.82,
          "en": "Now, if I add a goal, like finish the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 223.82,
          "end": 225.91,
          "en": "watch what happens when I press the button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 225.91,
          "end": 228.07,
          "en": "Watch here on the right side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 228.07,
          "end": 231.31,
          "en": "You see, now the unread list was added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 231.31,
          "end": 234.063,
          "en": "and the paragraph completely disappeared.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 234.98,
          "end": 237.35,
          "en": "Now, because of v-if and v-else combined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 237.35,
          "end": 240.8,
          "en": "by the way, Vue also doesn't need the place holder anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 240.8,
          "end": 242.72,
          "en": "But that's just a side note.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 242.72,
          "end": 243.71,
          "en": "So, that's v-if,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 243.71,
          "end": 246.1,
          "en": "and it's very, very, very useful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 246.1,
          "end": 248.21,
          "en": "for showing content conditionally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 248.21,
          "end": 251.13,
          "en": "which turns out is something you'll need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 251.13,
          "end": 253.77,
          "en": "in a lot of applications you're going to build.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 253.77,
          "end": 256.683,
          "en": "And, this is how easy it is to implement it with Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
